      "year": 2024,
      "abstract": "The beginning of the full-scale invasion of Russia on the territory of Ukraine forced a new look at the history of our country and the Ukrainian nation. On June 21, 2022, the National Agency for Quality Assurance of Higher Education issued a Decision in which special attention was paid to the historical and cultural component of the educational process. In this regard, a decision was made at the Izmail State University of Humanities to introduce new educational components and programs related to nation-building and national-patriotic education. The views on the nation-building process of the German researcher I.G. Fichte, which he expressed in \"Speeches to the German Nation\" (1808). The purpose of the article is to consider and investigate the processes of nation-building in the view of I.G. Fichte, based on his \"Speech to the German Nation\". It was Fichte who was the first to clearly realize that the real national self-determination of the people can be realized only with the help of their education. This basic position of the \"Speech to the German Nation\" is much more relevant today than two centuries ago, because nowadays the problem of national self-determination is not before one German people, as at the beginning of the 19th century, but in a certain sense before all peoples, if they do not want to to be involved in the third world war. It was found that the creation of a nation is the internal goal of the natural-historical development of a people, which ultimately realizes itself as a result of the process of educating its general identity, or national character, based on philosophical science. The necessity of national self-determination of a people lies in the fact that a people is born (that is, under certain natural conditions it historically becomes a people) precisely in order to be born anew in its spirit and truth, to become a real nation. That is why the true nation, according to Fichte, is a nation of a single people, and not a so-called \"civil nation\" of many citizens separated from each other. In the course of its development, the nation first finds the homeland and only then the fatherland, to which only the bright path of national education leads, which, on the basis of philosophy, consciously develops the potentially general feature of the spirit of the people into the actual generality of its reasonable attitude to nature, to itself and to other peoples.",
